Substantial modifications from the original Hypervibe Harness

Baudrier re-targets the plugin at a French-sovereign,
Scaleway-only architecture. Substantial changes include, without
limitation:

  - Removed: Vercel, Cloudflare (Workers, R2, DNS, Email Routing), Neon,
    Render, Resend, Brevo, Bitwarden, Stripe, Google/GitHub OAuth,
    internationalization (i18n), and inbound email receiving.

  - Added / re-targeted: hosting on Scaleway Serverless Containers
    (region fr-par) with images built and pushed directly by the harness
    (`docker build`/`docker push`, no CI) to Scaleway Container Registry;
    Scaleway Serverless SQL Database
    (PostgreSQL 16) with Drizzle ORM; Scaleway Object Storage
    (S3-compatible); Scaleway Domains & DNS; Scaleway Transactional
    Email (TEM); Scaleway Serverless Jobs for scheduling and AI agents;
    Scaleway Generative APIs for LLM and embeddings; Scaleway Secret
    Manager for secrets; Matomo for analytics.

  - The generated product is French-only (no i18n), and every scaffolded
    app is deployed IP-restricted to a company VPN by default.

